Title: THE WEIGHT OF WATER
Author: Ana Reyes
Draft date: June 2026

FADE IN:


INT. COUNTY FAMILY COURT - DAY

ELENA MORALES, 40s, sits beside her lawyer. Her ex-husband RICHARD fidgets with a SILVER WEDDING BAND on a chain.
JUDGE
Temporary custody remains with the mother pending evaluation.

INT. ELENA'S KITCHEN - NIGHT

Elena's daughter SOFIA, 12, does homework. Elena washes dishes, eyes on a stack of unpaid bills.
SOFIA
Dad said he'd pick me up Friday. Can he?
ELENA
We'll see what the court says. Eat your rice.

EXT. COMMUNITY POOL - DAY

Richard watches Sofia swim laps from the bleachers. Coach ALMA approaches.
ALMA
She's the fastest ten-year-old in the lane when she's not looking over her shoulder.
RICHARD
Tell me what she needs. Not what I want to hear.

INT. THERAPIST OFFICE - DAY

Elena and Richard sit on opposite ends of the couch. THERAPIST GINA takes notes.
GINA
Sofia said she feels like luggage. What do each of you hear in that?
ELENA
That we failed her in public and private.

EXT. COMMUNITY POOL - DUSK

Sofia sits between Elena and Richard on the bleachers. The SILVER BAND stays in Elena's pocket.
SOFIA
If I choose where to sleep, does that mean I stopped loving one of you?
Elena and Richard exchange a look — raw, ashamed, trying.
ELENA
No, mija. It means you're honest. We're the ones catching up.

FADE OUT.


THE END
